3.2 Scope 1, 2, and 3 (Q17, Q18, Q19)
Scope 1: Direct emissions (fuel logs). CarbonTally’s CSV/OCR handles this well.
Scope 2: Indirect energy (utility bills). OCR extraction of PDF bills is a core strength.
Scope 3: Value chain. This is the hardest. CarbonTally’s spend-based mapping via CSV uploads addresses Category 1 (Purchased Goods) and Category 8 (Upstream Leased Assets) effectively.
3.3 DEFRA Compatibility (Q20)
Status: Highly Compatible. DEFRA factors are the gold standard for UK reporting and widely respected in Ireland/EU for lack of local alternatives.
Evidence: DEFRA updates conversion factors annually (e.g., 2025/2026 updates reflect a 14.5% drop in UK electricity factors, which platforms must dynamically update to avoid "false progress" reporting) 
www.compareyourfootprint.com
, 
www.acclaro-advisory.com
. CarbonTally’s 1,500 curated factors must be updated annually to maintain viability.
